; ted-outmem-blitz2-init (#1008): out of memory in blitz2's start-up
; calls of TED's services, before TED's main loop: outmem continues with
; memstack, which is 0 there (a7 = 0).  blitz2 under inject (alerts
; answered), the allocation of the initial object buffers (makeiallox:
; the four default sizes, 57344 bytes, MEMF_PUBLIC|MEMF_CLEAR) fails
; once; then CREATE EXECUTABLE, QUIT.  Correct: the alert "Not enough
; memory for operation!", the start goes on (version requester), the
; compile allocates the buffers and creates the executable, blitz2 ends
; normally; the original continues with a7 = 0 and crashes.
; @file bo.bas "NPrint \"hello\"\n"
; @source F bo.bas
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject alerts allocfail=57344-57344/f=10001/1 blitz2:blitz2 @FILE@
; @expect stdout "inject: allocfail: 1 allocations failed"
; @expect stdout "inject: alert: Not enough memory for operation!"
; @expect stdout "inject: rc=0"
; @expect exists bo
timeout 20
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
menu 4 2
wait freq "Name of Executable to create"
timeout 30
freq ok "bo" "TEDRUN:work"  ; @ignore compilewindow
timeout 10
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
